  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$\nand\n$A^{-1}=\\frac{1}{k} \\operatorname{adj}(A)$....(i)\nWe know that, $A^{-1}=\\frac{\\operatorname{adj}(A)}{|A|}$...(ii)\nBy comparing Eqs. (i) and (iii),\n$k=|A|$\nSo,\n$\\begin{aligned}\n|A| & =\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}\n3 & -2 & 4 \\\\\n1 & 2 & -1 \\\\\n0 & 1 & 1\n\\end{array}\\right| \\\\\n& =3(2+1)+2(1+0)+4(1-0)=15\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
